    feat(growth): Meta/Google OAuth foundation and Growth MCP read namespace
    
    OAUTH (src/lib/growth/connectors/oauth.ts)
    Code-complete Meta and Google handshake: state minting with constant-time
    verification, capability-to-scope mapping, URL construction, token exchange, and
    connection-state derivation. Needs no credential to build or test.
    
    - State is stored hashed and single-use, and expires on a clock rather than a
      cleanup job, so a stale handshake cannot be replayed.
    - Callers request a capability, never a raw scope string, so least privilege is
      the default rather than something an operator has to remember.
    - Exchange returns a secret reference, never a token. SecretStore is an interface
      because 'no token ever reaches a caller' is a property of the interface, not of
      whichever store is configured.
    - Google requests access_type=offline and prompt=consent. Without them Google
      returns no refresh token and the connection silently dies after an hour.
    - deriveConnectionState makes CONNECTED unreachable without a verification time,
      mirroring the schema constraint, so an unverified green connection is not
      representable.
    - A malformed request reports INVALID_INPUT, not 'not configured'. Telling an
      operator to set an environment variable when their request was malformed sends
      them to the wrong place.
    
    MCP GATEWAY (D:\\KNOUX-MCP-Gateway\\growth_tools.py, test_growth_tools.py)
    21 read-only Growth capabilities, registered only if not on an explicit
    never-register list of 8 mutating ids. 9/9 behavioural tests pass.
    
    The tests assert refusals rather than return values: unconfigured reads return
    NOT_CONFIGURED instead of an empty list, credentials-without-authorisation return
    AUTH_REQUIRED, every result carries changes_made False, and the manifest reports
    IMPLEMENTED 21 / VERIFIED 0.
    
    One test caught a real defect in my own module: connection_status reported
    lowercase short names while the actual variables are uppercase, so the diagnostic
    would have told an operator to set a variable that does not exist. Now maps to
    real env names.
    
    NOT DEPLOYED. Nothing was registered on a running gateway and no provider call
    was made. REGISTERED/DISCOVERABLE/AUTHENTICATED/EXECUTED/VERIFIED are all 0.

